# ============================================================
#  Expansion — Summer recess (months 11–12).
#  `has(summer_away)` = went home / travelled; otherwise you're
#  at the near-empty academy or working in the village.
# ============================================================

@event sum_empty_castle
title: The Empty Castle
class: routine
tone: eerie
when: month >= 11 and not has(summer_away)
weight: 16
art: tower
tags: mystery home
scene: A vast empty dining hall in summer, chairs upturned on the tables, a single student eating alone in a shaft of dusty sunlight.
text: In summer the castle breathes differently. Corridors you've walked a thousand times are silent; doors that are always locked stand slightly open. A portrait yawns. Nobody is watching.
> left: Explore the open doors
  challenge deceive trivial:
    win:
      lore +medium
      gold +small
      say: Behind one door: a forgotten trophy room. Behind another: a professor's stash of very old toffee and a purse of lost-property coins nobody will miss.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: Behind the first door: the caretaker, in a dressing gown, very surprised. You both agree this never happened.
> right: Enjoy the quiet
  mood +medium
  health +small
  say: You read in window seats, nap on the great lawn and eat breakfast at noon. For two weeks the most famous academy in the kingdom is just a big, peaceful house.

@event sum_home_chores
title: Help Around the House
class: routine
tone: warm
when: month >= 11 and has(summer_away) and not has(origin_noble)
weight: 14
art: house
tags: home
scene: A farmhouse kitchen in high summer, a basket of laundry, a list of chores pinned to the door, a textbook hidden under a tea towel.
text: Home is lovely for about three days. Then the list appears on the kitchen door: the roof, the goats, the fence, the cousin's wedding. Your summer reading list is hidden under a tea towel.
> left: Do the chores — with magic
  challenge spell trivial:
    win:
      mood +small
      renown +small
      say: The fence mends itself, the goats are briefly levitated, the roof is better than new. The whole street comes to watch. Your mother pretends not to be proud.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: The goats are briefly levitated. Unfortunately so is the fence. Your family is very patient about it.
> right: Do them the slow way, and talk
  mood +small
  vigor +small
  say: You fix the fence by hand with your father, saying very little and then, suddenly, a lot. It's the best conversation you've had all year.

@event sum_old_friend
title: An Old Friend
class: windfall
tone: warm
when: month >= 11 and has(summer_away)
weight: 12
art: group
tags: social home
scene: Two young people sitting on a stone wall above a village, one in academy robes, one in work clothes, a little space between them.
text: Your oldest friend from home is waiting at the crossroads, like always. But something's different. "So," they say, not quite looking at you, "I suppose you're too grand for us now."
> left: Prove you're not
  mood +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You spend the summer exactly as you used to — orchard raids, river swims, terrible jokes. By Starfall, the space between you on the wall is gone.
> right: Admit you've changed
  lore +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: "I have," you say. "So have you." They laugh, surprised. You talk all night about who you're both becoming. It's different from before. It might be better.

@event sum_midsummer_fair
title: The Midsummer Fair
class: routine
tone: light
when: month == 11 or month == 12
weight: 12
art: tent
tags: festival money
scene: A village green full of striped tents, a carousel of enchanted wooden animals, lanterns strung between trees, a strongman lifting a cow.
text: The village Midsummer Fair: enchanted carousel, ring-toss, a strongman, and a booth promising "GUESS YOUR WEIGHT IN CHEESE". You have a few crowns in your pocket and a whole afternoon.
> left: Win something at the ring-toss (Vigor)
  challenge feat trivial:
    win:
      gold +medium
      mood +small
      say: Three rings, three hits. You win a stuffed griffon the size of a sheep and sell it to a crying child's father for fifteen crowns. Everyone wins.
    lose:
      gold -tiny
      mood +tiny
      say: Every ring bounces off. The ring-toss is definitely enchanted. You don't care; you're eating candied apples.
> right: Ride the carousel
  gold -tiny
  mood +medium
  say: Your wooden hippogriff takes off, very slightly, at the top of every turn. You ride it nine times.

@event sum_letter_from_friend
title: A Summer Letter
class: windfall
tone: light
trigger: social
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 20 and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
when: month >= 11
art: letter
tags: social
scene: A thick letter with a doodle on the envelope arriving by owl at a summer window.
text: An owl arrives with a thick, slightly crumpled letter from {npc}. Six pages of summer news, two doodles, one pressed flower, and at the end, in smaller writing: "I miss the castle. I miss you, actually."
> left: Write a short reply
  rel npc +small
  say: You write a page. It's warm, if brief. {npc} keeps it anyway.
> right: Write back for hours
  rel npc +medium
  mood +small
  say: You write until the candle gutters. Twelve pages. You can't remember the last time you wrote that much that wasn't an essay.

@event sum_rain_week
title: A Week of Rain
class: routine
tone: warm
when: month >= 11
weight: 10
art: rain
tags: home
scene: Rain streaming down a tall window, a student curled in an armchair with a fat novel, a teapot steaming on the sill.
text: It rains for a solid week. Not dramatic rain: just steady, grey, endless rain. Every plan you made for the summer is quietly drowning.
> left: Read a very long novel
  mood +small
  lore +tiny
  say: You read eight hundred pages about a family of sea-witches and cry at the end. It's the best week of the summer.
> right: Practise spells indoors
  arcana +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You practise until you can light every candle in the room with a flick. You also set fire to one curtain. It's raining; it goes out quickly.

@event sum_sea_serpent
title: Fishing With an Uncle
class: routine
tone: tense
when: month >= 11 and has(summer_away)
weight: 8
art: wave
tags: nature danger
scene: A small fishing boat on a grey-green sea, a fishing line drawn taut, something very long and scaled rising beside the hull.
text: Your uncle takes you fishing. Something takes the bait. Something very large. The line sings. The boat tilts. A long scaled neck rises out of the water and looks at you with polite interest.
> left: Cut the line
  mood +tiny
  say: The serpent sinks back with a sigh like a disappointed whale. Your uncle tells the story for the rest of his life, and it gets bigger every time.
> right: Try to talk to it (Charm)
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      lore +medium
      renown +small
      say: You greet it in the old courtesies Professor Brask taught you. It bows its great head, leaves a pearl on the deck and swims away. Your uncle faints.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: The serpent is not interested in conversation. It is interested in the boat. You swim home.

@event sum_reading_list
title: The Summer Reading List
class: routine
tone: light
when: month == 11
weight: 12
art: scroll
tags: study
scene: A long scroll unrolling off a table and across the floor, a list of titles in tiny handwriting, a student staring at it in despair.
text: The summer reading list arrives by owl. It is a scroll. It unrolls across the floor, out of the door and partway down the stairs. Thorne has added a note at the bottom: "Optional. (It is not optional.)"
> left: Read all of it
  lore +medium
  study +medium
  mood -small
  say: You read everything. When term starts, Thorne asks a question about the last book and you're the only one who can answer. His eyebrow rises half a millimetre.
> right: Read the first and last chapters of each
  guile +tiny
  study +tiny
  say: A time-honoured strategy. You can talk confidently about the beginning and end of forty books. The middle remains a mystery, like most of life.

@event sum_night_market
title: The Night Market
class: routine
tone: eerie
when: month >= 11 and gold >= 15
weight: 10
art: lantern
tags: money mystery
scene: A market that only appears after midnight, stalls lit with coloured flames, hooded sellers, a bottle that seems to contain a small thundercloud.
text: A night market appears in a field outside the village — it wasn't there yesterday and won't be tomorrow. A hooded stall-keeper offers you a stoppered bottle with a tiny thundercloud inside. "Fifteen crowns. What it does is a surprise."
> left: Buy the bottle
  gold -medium
  chance 50:
    gain inspired
    arcana +small
    say: You uncork it in your room. The little storm rains ideas on you for a fortnight. Your notebooks overflow.
  else:
    mood -tiny
    gain sick
    say: You uncork it in your room. The little storm rains on you. Just rain. For a fortnight. You catch a cold.
> right: Just look around
  mood +small
  lore +tiny
  say: You wander until dawn, buying nothing, watching everything. When the sun rises the field is empty except for a single glowing feather. You keep it.

@event sum_end_of_summer
title: The Last Week of Summer
class: windfall
tone: warm
when: month == 12
weight: 14
art: sun
tags: home
scene: A student packing a trunk in golden late-summer light, a half-finished jar of jam, a pressed flower and a new textbook on the bed.
text: The last week of summer has that particular light — golden, heavy, already nostalgic. Your trunk is half-packed. Part of you is desperate to get back. Part of you wants this week to last forever.
> left: Squeeze every drop out of it
  mood +medium
  health +tiny
  say: Late swims, long dinners, one final sunset from the hill. You arrive at the barge sunburnt and happy and only slightly late.
> right: Get ready for the new year
  study +small
  lore +tiny
  say: You re-read your notes, sharpen your quills and polish your wand. When term starts you are, for once, ahead. It's an unfamiliar feeling.
